# What was built. Only the artifacts: one file per composition.
/build/

# How they were built — the generated C++, the build system that turns it into an
# artifact, and the tree the toolchain leaves behind. Rewritten in full on every run.
/.bareruby/

# The SDKs and toolchains the APIs build with, downloaded or built in place: one
# directory per API, plus common/ for what more than one of them reaches for, and every
# version in its name. Here because the build reaches for them; out of git because they
# are other people's releases.
/.tools/

# Which boards are on this desk is a fact about a desk, not about this repository.
# Copy config/target.yml.sample to start one. In a project written by `bareruby new` this
# file is tracked instead: which compositions a project is built for is true of it.
/config/target.yml

# Gems this checkout reaches for, installed here rather than into the desk.
/.gems/

# The lock this checkout resolves for itself. Every gem in it is read from gems/ in the
# working tree, so what a lock would pin is the handful of released gems underneath them,
# and re-resolving is how a change to a gemspec is noticed at all.
/Gemfile.lock

# The extension, packed. `vscode/package.sh` writes it and VS Code installs it; the
# sources beside it are what is kept.
/vscode/*.vsix
